#X obj 574 11 ui.link @background_color 0.39216 0.39216 0.39216 @title
[ceammc/bitmap] @url bitmap-help.pd;
#X obj 696 8 bitmap;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 282 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object stores a binary image as a 2D matrix of bits
and provides a set of drawing \, transformation and I/O methods. The
bitmap size is set with the W and H arguments (or the @w and @h properties)
and cannot be changed after creation. Pixels can be drawn with drawing
methods (line \, rect \, circle \, text and others) \, transformed
(mirror \, shift \, invert) \, loaded from an image file or set from
a list or matrix. The content can be output as a list or as a [matrix
NROWS NCOLS DATA...( message \, saved as a PNG file \, and viewed in
a separate window.;
#X text 240 244 Colors: the bitmap is binary \, so pixels have only
two possible values — 0 or 1\. Drawing methods use the fill color (@fill_color)
or the stroke color (@stroke_color) if they draw outlines. Color can
be 0 or 1 \, or -1 for "no color" (for fill_color and text_color).
The method fill sets all pixels to a given value at once.;
